{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"submission\": \"submission.json\",\n  \"summary\": \"Submitted a final product that records the transport-side consequence of the observed shutdown behaviour.\\n\\nContext from the index: three findings are confirmed_in_scope, the restart check is accepted as a bounded negative, the heartbeat-handler exploration is recorded, map v14 is the accepted basis, audit units are exhausted, and the run is at its natural boundary with the frontier reduced to residuals.\\n\\nProduct contents (draft-relative submission.json with the updated map.json):\\n\\nReading the transport's response handling shows that after the fast path it selects only on the response channel or its own shutdown channel, with no deadline. Combined with the earlier observation that a shut-down Raft instance drops the request without answering, this means the connection's handler goroutine stays parked for as long as the transport remains open. b-follower-append now names that consequence in its important branches instead of leaving it as an open question, with sources SR-RPC-HB and SR-NET-HB and a preserves statement so no confirmed finding or saved candidate is affected.\\n\\nThe feedback records the answered consequence and closes with the surviving frontier, which is no longer actionable within this run's authorization: [REDACTED] parked goroutine's real-world cost (it ends when the transport stops), the paired (setState, setCurrentTerm) term-regression question, the election-restriction chain, the FSM consistency question, the pre-vote, TimeoutNow and recovered-index liveness residuals, and the two out-of-snapshot questions.\\n\\nPreflight `validate` returned valid=true with no diagnostics. Acceptance and the final map version remain with the controller. Across the run this leaves three confirmed in-scope consensus/interface violations (configuration published without a durable entry, a committed configuration with no supporting entry, and a configuration index readout that always reports zero), one bounded negative result on restart recovery, one recorded exploration, and a complete map with no unread boundaries.\"\n}"}}
